  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_008 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, weighted) is the current best at 0.532 acc / 0.516 F1, slightly ahead of config_018 (same but resnet50, 0.523). RNA is clearly the dominant modality (0.485 alone vs 0.208 for image), and pca_n2000 substantially outperforms scgpt (0.523 vs 0.421). The only fusion strategy tested so far is 'weighted'; we have no evidence about whether 'concat' could be superior. Question: config_021 is identical to config_008 except fusion changes from weighted to concat, giving a clean single-variable comparison to isolate the effect of fusion strategy with the best-known encoder pair. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly extends the strongest result with a minimal change, reducing uncertainty about whether a different fusion mechanism could push performance higher before we invest budget in more complex multiprofile/aggregation designs. If concat matches or beats weighted, it reshapes the design space; if it underperforms, it confirms weighted as the preferred fusion and lets us focus subsequent experiments on profile setting and aggregation."
}

